Package: alist
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd
Recommends: ffmpeg
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://alistgo.com
Description: AList File Manager - aggregate cloud drives with WebDAV
 AList is a self-hosted file list program that aggregates many storage
 backends (local folders, WebDAV, S3-compatible object storage and dozens
 of cloud drives) behind one clean web UI: browse, preview, upload,
 download, share, offline-download, plus a built-in WebDAV server so any
 client can mount all your storages as one drive.
 .
 The web UI opens in a new browser tab via the TOS App Center route
 /alist/. The backend listens on loopback only: no external port is
 exposed. The first-install admin password is generated automatically
 and stored root-readable in /var/lib/alist/admin_password.txt
 (username: admin, change it after login).
 Database, temp files and search index are stored in /var/lib/alist;
 'apt remove' keeps them, 'apt purge' deletes them.
 .
 Upstream: https://github.com/AlistGo/alist (AGPL-3.0)
 Upstream author: AList Team. Packaged for TOS by the deb Maintainer.
